import{_ as o,o as n,c as t,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 762 | Hyper-Multiverse-Grade Civilizational Engineering | Cross-Cosmos Anchor-Network Construction","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 762 | Hyper-Multiverse-Grade Civilizational Engineering | Cross-Cosmos Anchor-Network Construction","no":762,"module":4,"tags":["Hyper-Multiverse-Grade Civilizational Engineering","Cross-Cosmos Anchor Network","Anchor Connection","Myriad-Rank Symbiosis","Infrastructure"],"related":["28-Cross-Plane Anchor Connection","20-Anchor Structure and Hierarchy","78-Cross-Plane Exploration Era"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0762_模块4-超多元级文明工程-跨宇宙锚点网络.md","filePath":"en/0762_模块4-超多元级文明工程-跨宇宙锚点网络.md"}'),s={name:"en/0762_模块4-超多元级文明工程-跨宇宙锚点网络.md"};function r(a,e,l,c,h,u){return n(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i(`<h1 id="entry-762-hyper-multiverse-grade-civilizational-engineering-cross-cosmos-anchor-network-construction" tabindex="-1">Entry 762 | Hyper-Multiverse-Grade Civilizational Engineering | Cross-Cosmos Anchor-Network Construction <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-762-hyper-multiverse-grade-civilizational-engineering-cross-cosmos-anchor-network-construction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 762 | Hyper-Multiverse-Grade Civilizational Engineering | Cross-Cosmos Anchor-Network Construction&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 28, 20, 78</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-connect-isolated-cosmos-into-one-network" tabindex="-1">Introduction: connect isolated cosmos into one network <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-connect-isolated-cosmos-into-one-network" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: connect isolated cosmos into one network&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s ultimate infrastructure is not some plane&#39;s spirit-vein network, not some multiverse&#39;s anchor system, but the <strong>cross-cosmos anchor network</strong> — connecting different multiverses through living anchors, forming a symbiotic network covering all known cosmos. This is the grandest project in civilizational engineering, and also the key step for Myriad-Rank Republic to upgrade from &quot;one cosmos&#39;s republic&quot; to &quot;multi-cosmos republic.&quot;</p><p>Six top-level axioms here are network construction&#39;s skeleton: the anti-predation axiom requires the network transmit only increment; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires every cosmos&#39;s civilization have a node; the collective ascension axiom requires the network accelerate collective uplift; the causal self-discipline axiom requires inter-cosmos connections not disturb each other&#39;s causality; the law-first axiom requires network protocols be self-consistent.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-why-the-cross-cosmos-anchor-network-is-needed" tabindex="-1">I. Why the Cross-Cosmos Anchor Network Is Needed <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-why-the-cross-cosmos-anchor-network-is-needed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Why the Cross-Cosmos Anchor Network Is Needed&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A single cosmos&#39;s anchor network, no matter how complete, has a ceiling:</p><ul><li><strong>Resources finite</strong>: a single cosmos&#39;s matter, energy, and law resources are finite;</li><li><strong>Isolation risk</strong>: if one cosmos has a problem, there is no external support;</li><li><strong>Knowledge islands</strong>: different cosmos&#39;s civilizations do not know each other&#39;s existence;</li><li><strong>Predation escape</strong>: after predatory factions are driven out of one cosmos, they may escape to another.</li></ul><p>The cross-cosmos anchor network solves these four problems: resource interflow, disaster mutual rescue, knowledge sharing, predators nowhere to flee.</p><h2 id="ii-the-network-s-three-layer-architecture" tabindex="-1">II. The Network&#39;s Three-Layer Architecture <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-network-s-three-layer-architecture" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Network&#39;s Three-Layer Architecture&quot;">​</a></h2><div class="language- vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span>Layer 3: Cross-Cosmos Backbone Network</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  ← backbone anchors connecting different multiverses</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Layer 2: Intra-Multiverse Network</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  ← inter-plane network inside each multiverse</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Layer 1: Plane Local Network</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  ← inter-city-state network inside each plane</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The three-layer network interconnects step by step from local to cross-cosmos. This entry focuses on Layer 3.</p><h2 id="iii-backbone-anchor-selection-criteria" tabindex="-1">III. Backbone Anchor Selection Criteria <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-backbone-anchor-selection-criteria" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Backbone Anchor Selection Criteria&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Cross-cosmos backbone anchors are not chosen at random; their criteria are extremely strict:</p><ul><li>Cultivator has reached the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm;</li><li>Civilizational weight ranks in Myriad Ranks&#39; top 0.01%;</li><li>Heart-nature tested for 10,000+ years, no predatory record;</li><li>Rich cross-cosmos operation experience;</li><li>Passed by Myriad-Rank representative vote.</li></ul><p>Every backbone anchor is Myriad Ranks&#39; most reliable node, tested over ten thousand years and through countless events.</p><h2 id="iv-network-protocol-rules-of-cross-cosmos-communication" tabindex="-1">IV. Network Protocol: Rules of Cross-Cosmos Communication <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-network-protocol-rules-of-cross-cosmos-communication" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Network Protocol: Rules of Cross-Cosmos Communication&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The cross-cosmos anchor network follows strict network protocols:</p><ul><li><strong>Transmit knowledge, not intervention</strong>: cosmos share knowledge, technology, and early warnings, but do not directly interfere with each other&#39;s internal affairs;</li><li><strong>Observe-first-then-contact</strong>: before a new cosmos joins the network, observe first then contact;</li><li><strong>Peer connection</strong>: every cosmos node in the network has equal status; there is no &quot;big-brother cosmos&quot;;</li><li><strong>Disconnection right</strong>: any cosmos, if it believes the network connection harms its interests, may apply to disconnect, but must go through consultation procedure.</li></ul><p>After the cross-cosmos backbone network is built, the real test is O&amp;M. Distances between backbone anchors are measured in cosmic eons; law-parameter drift at any one node may cause the entire network to oscillate. Therefore, Heng Yuan Zhou additionally sets up &quot;Watcher Node Clusters&quot; outside the backbone network — composed of dozens of lower-order plane-supreme strong ones forming a rotating team, monitoring 24/7 the backbone anchors&#39; energy waveforms, law compatibility, and information latency. Once some backbone node shows anomaly, the Watchers complete initial judgment within half a cosmic eon, then nearby transcended-one teams intervene to calibrate. Bandwidth allocation is not egalitarian: newly joined cosmos enjoy bandwidth tilt in the first three eons, helping their civilization quickly catch up; mature cosmos&#39; bandwidth returns to baseline, yielding resources to rising cosmos. This dynamic scheduling avoids the Matthew effect of &quot;old cosmos always occupying the main road, new cosmos unable to get on the fast lane,&quot; keeping the cross-cosmos network always weak-tilted in its public attribute.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: isolated cosmos fight separately, with massive duplicate construction; the cross-cosmos network lets knowledge, resources, and experience be shared network-wide</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: after predatory factions are driven out of one cosmos, they have nowhere to flee, because the whole network is linked</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: the Tang-Luo system&#39;s &quot;cross-cosmos&quot; is Gu Chensha alone going wherever he wants; Heng Yuan Zhou is a co-built, shared network</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: every cosmos&#39;s Myriad Ranks have their own node representatives, not humankind cosmos calling the shots</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: network protocols, access standards, and data formats are all public network-wide through the Selfless Dao</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The cross-cosmos anchor network is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s &quot;Myriad-Rank Republic&quot; idea&#39;s infrastructure for expanding from one cosmos to multi-cosmos. It is not conquering other cosmos, but connecting other cosmos — linking isolated islands into a continent, linking separately-fighting civilizations into a community of shared destiny.</p><blockquote><p>Terminology note: the practices described in this entry ultimately land on Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm perpetual-construction posts. Every cultivator participating in engineering has his contribution recorded in real time by Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision, automatically settling civilizational weight. All engineering design uses the law-first axiom as meta-rule, ensuring the 300-set Origin Cultivation System coordinates at hyper-multiverse scale without self-contradiction.</p></blockquote><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/28-跨位面锚点连接.html">Entry 28 · Cross-Plane Anchor Connection</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/20-锚点结构与层级.html">Entry 20 · Anchor Structure and Hierarchy</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/78-跨位面探索纪元.html">Entry 78 · Cross-Plane Exploration Era</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/24-锚点能量传导路径.html">Entry 24 · Anchor Energy-Conduction Path</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>`,28)])])}const p=o(s,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
